  "limitations": [
    "The data is synthetic. The four engineered features copy the generator's label rules (oracle-informed), so class separation is easier than in real data.",
    "100% High recall (224/224 in cross-validation, 44/44 on test) is an observed result, not a guarantee; one missed High record changes the test cost by $1,000.",
    "The deployment threshold was chosen on pooled out-of-fold training scores; the nested outer-fold result is the less biased estimate of the selection procedure.",
    "SDCA scores are not separately calibrated; the threshold is valid only for this model's score semantics.",
    "Several configurations were compared on the same folds; small differences (e.g. F1 0.815 vs 0.822) are within fold noise.",
    "The older CalculateMetricsForThreshold reads Score[1] (Medium in this harness); the Chapter 6 code does not use it."
  ]
